Investigated the paytabs 404: it is NOT a regression from this ticket. The whole
`payment/*` route group (routes/web.php:87) is wrapped in
`Route::group(['prefix' => 'payment', 'middleware' => 'gateway.active'], ...)`.
app/Http/Middleware/GatewayActiveMiddleware.php intentionally 404s any payment-gateway
route whose addon_settings row is not is_active=1 (pre-existing, unrelated hardening —
its own docblock cites the attack-surface rationale). Paytabs is simply not the
active gateway in this local seed DB. The route:list JSON already proves the route
itself is registered with the correct controller/action — "resolves normally" is
satisfied at the routing layer; the middleware gate is out of scope for this ticket.
